// Title: Use of Pcalua For Execution
// Sigma ID: 0955e4e1-c281-4fb9-9ee1-5ee7b4b754d2
// Status: test | Level: medium
// Author: Nasreddine Bencherchali (Nextron Systems), E.M. Anhaus (originally from Atomic Blue Detections, Endgame), oscd.community
// Date: 2022-06-14 | Modified: 2023-01-04
// ATT&CK: execution, T1059
// Description: Detects execition of commands and binaries from the context of The program compatibility
//   assistant (Pcalua.exe). This can be used as a LOLBIN in order to bypass application
//   whitelisting.
// False positives:
//   - Legitimate use by a via a batch script or by an administrator.
// References:
//   - https://lolbas-project.github.io/lolbas/Binaries/Pcalua/
//   - https://pentestlab.blog/2020/07/06/indirect-command-execution/
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/05d1031f537e830b76da53bae2400c5814c89165/rules/windows/process_creation/proc_creation_win_lolbin_pcalua.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language 12.4.1, microsoft_xdr schema)

DeviceProcessEvents
| where FolderPath endswith "\\pcalua.exe" and ProcessCommandLine contains " -a"
